\subsection{Other Requirements}

The application requires a configured MongoDB connection, a JWT secret, and the appropriate runtime environment variables. Sensitive configuration values should not be committed to the source repository.

Automated unit and integration test suites are not part of the current implementation and are identified as future improvements.

\subsection*{Requirement Traceability}

The requirements are reflected across multiple software layers. Authentication requirements are implemented through the authentication routes, controller, User model, JWT generation, and frontend authentication context. Operational requirements are implemented through individual route groups, controllers, models, and frontend resource pages.

This traceability is useful during testing because a requirement can be checked at both the API and user-interface levels. For example, a flight creation requirement can be tested by directly calling the API and by submitting the corresponding frontend form.


